kitty-image-replay

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: Keep kitty images and their placements in the core, loading file, temporary-file and shared-memory media on the core's own machine and PNG through the png crate, and send viewers images, never names: a transmission by path reaches viewers as PNG, and every repaint (attach, reattach, catch-up, another machine) re-sends the stored images with their placements, on screen and in the history it replays. Encodings are cached per image generation, and a viewer's empty queue takes a repaint whole however large.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream herdr-core stores kitty images and replays them to viewers that attach, as pixels.
